OpenRevo EC driver for Ubuntu and Debian
======================================

This package contains the source for the model-verified OpenRevo EC driver.
It requires headers matching the kernel you intend to use. DKMS builds and
installs the module for available kernels and rebuilds it after kernel upgrades.
Read installation output: missing kernel headers can defer the module build.

Secure Boot signing uses the distribution's DKMS configuration and keys.
Complete its MOK enrollment procedure if requested. This package does not
disable Secure Boot, generate its own signing policy, or enroll keys silently.

The application and driver must support the same control ABI. Close the
application and reboot after an upgrade to activate the newly built module.
Package installation and removal never force an active module to unload.

Old manual installations under /lib/modules/<kernel>/extra/openrevo must be
resolved before configuring this package. Its maintainer scripts report such
files and leave them intact. Do not operate two copies of the controller.

Run the graphical application as the desktop user. The udev rule grants device
access to the active local session. The driver itself limits the supported
machine and BIOS and validates hardware commands. Unknown models remain
unsupported by the EC module; standard Linux telemetry is independent of it.
